# width: 120
# `ui.dock.mode = .auto_hide`, the shipped default: nothing is drawn
# until the pointer has rested on the SCREEN's last row — the `:`
# line's row, row 39 at 120x40 — for `ui.dock.reveal_ms` (250 ms), and
# the strip goes again `ui.dock.hide_ms` (400 ms) after the pointer
# leaves. The edge a hand reaches for is the frame's own whichever
# placement is in force; under the default `.inner` the strip then
# PAINTS two rows up, over the editor area's last row, leaving the
# statusline and the `:` line alone (`launcher_dock_placement.test`).
#
# It draws OVER the editor — it never re-lays-out, the rule
# `app/sidebar_auto.zig` already lives by — so the marker at column 95
# of the open file is on screen the whole time.
write wide.txt "...............................................................................................ENDMARK\n"
open wide.txt
# The tree closed, so the editor spans the frame and the marker at
# column 95 is on screen: a reveal that re-laid-out would take it away.
command view.toggle_tree
expect screen contains "ENDMARK"
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
# The dwell: the pointer rests on row 39.
hover 60 39
wait 600
expect screen contains "New terminal"
expect screen contains "ENDMARK"
# Resting on the strip itself keeps it up — the painter registers it as
# the second piece of its own hover zone.
hover 20 39
wait 600
expect screen contains "New terminal"
# Away: gone after the hide dwell.
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
# The pin keeps it: a pinned strip docks and stays wherever the pointer
# goes, and unpinning hands it back to `ui.dock.mode`.
hover 60 39
wait 600
expect screen contains "New terminal"
command view.dock_pin
expect screen contains "dock pinned"
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen contains "New terminal"
command view.dock_pin
expect screen contains "dock: auto_hide"
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
